Writer and founder of //Low-tech Magazine//.

In 2018 he rebuilt the magazine's website with [[Marie Otsuka]] and [[Roel Roscam Abbing]] to run on a small solar panel and a battery. The pages are static. The images are dithered. There are no trackers.

When the battery runs out, the site goes offline until the sun comes back.

Does a website need to be open all night?

See [[Solar.LowTechMagazine.com]], [[Permacomputing]], [[Scalability downwards is more significant]]
